\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.12}{\ignorespaces \texttt  {simp\_once}: \texttt  {Seq}/\texttt  {Alt} simplification for annotated expressions. \texttt  {Seq} removes dead ($\emptyset $) or already-\texttt  {Eps} operands, while \texttt  {Alt} removes dead and duplicate branches. Removed bits are transferred using \texttt  {fuse\_bits}, the \texttt  {Bits}-native counterpart of \texttt  {fuse} (Section~\ref {sec:fuse}), avoiding a slice conversion and copy of the accumulated bit history. }}{35}{figure.caption.27}\protected@file@percent }
